From: alvesmaicon <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: sun8i-codec: power the path down pmdown_time after a stream

The A33 codec's component had no use_pmdown_time, so the card powered
the whole path down as each stream closed. Every sound then waited for
the headphone amplifier's 700 ms power up, and the closing program
waited for the power down.

With use_pmdown_time the power down runs in a worker pmdown_time (5 s by
default) after the last stream: sounds close together keep the path up,
and nothing waits for the power down.

diff --git a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun8i-codec.c b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun8i-codec.c
index 4b60203..8525912 100644
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun8i-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun8i-codec.c
@@ -1671,6 +1671,7 @@ static const struct snd_soc_component_driver sun8i_soc_component = {
 	.probe			= sun8i_codec_component_probe,
 	.idle_bias_on		= 1,
 	.suspend_bias_off	= 1,
+	.use_pmdown_time	= 1,
 	.endianness		= 1,
 };
 
